    "result_text": "The full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented customerCode collision de-duplication with minimal structural impact.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **New file** `OwnerCustomerCodeDeduplicator.java` \u2014 a small, cohesive `@Component` (empty surrounding context) that holds the `OwnerRepository` and exposes one method `unique(base)`: it gathers the customerCodes already in use, and if `base` is taken, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that is free, returning the de-duplicated code.\n- **`OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice.java`** \u2014 added a field + constructor to inject the deduplicator, and changed the single `setCustomerCode(...)` line to pass the computed code through `deduplicator.unique(...)`.\n\n**Why this shape:** the collision rule lives in its own unit rather than expanding the aspect's `assignCustomerCode` method (CC\u22486). The only edit to that method is one line, and the new numbering/lookup logic sits in a fresh class with no surrounding complexity \u2014 keeping every changed function simple and its WMC_other low.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
